From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pedro Maione <pedro.maione@9elements.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:28:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fansensor: move fan inventory item out of TachSensor

TachSensor publishes the inventory item of a fan that has a presence
GPIO, and updates its Present property from the tach read loop. A fan
without a tachometer has no TachSensor, so it cannot get an item.

Move the item into a FanItem class that polls the presence GPIO on its
own timer. TachSensor still marks itself unavailable while the fan is
absent. Start the GPIO monitor once when it is created instead of in
every TachSensor that shares it, which restarted the monitor of a
shared GPIO each time.

The published objects and properties are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
